uthorized users map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to one or more pens, retain allocated animal quantities, and display the resulting traceability and pen information.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-25\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The import response identifies source records as matched to existing records\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen displays the matched record list and response status without displaying those records as newly created duplicates\",\n     \"when\": \"The repeated import completes\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A repeated-import response updates a PO line's head count below its existing mapped allocation quantities and returns an allocation conflict\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen displays the matched record, returned head count, existing mapped quantities, and an allocation-conflict flag without presenting the record as a new duplicate\",\n     \"when\": \"The repeated import completes\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an operational user repeats an import containing previously imported source-system identifiers, the feedlot web app shall display the import result for the matched records returned by the import service without presenting them as newly created duplicates, and flag returned allocation conflicts when an updated head count is below existing mapped quantities.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"ASM-24\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and a lot-specific override\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen displays the returned in